  "notes": "WRITING:\n- {停|てい} - stop, halt\n- {滞|たい} - stagnate, be delayed\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {経済|けいざい}の{停滞|ていたい} - economic stagnation\n- {停滞|ていたい}{状態|じょうたい} - state of stagnation\n- {停滞|ていたい}{前線|ぜんせん} - stationary front (weather)\n- {停滞|ていたい}が{続|つづ}く - stagnation continues\n- {停滞|ていたい}を{打破|だは}する - to break through stagnation\n\nWEATHER TERM:\n{停滞前線|ていたいぜんせん} - stationary front. A weather front that has stopped moving, often causing prolonged rain.\n\nCONTRASTING TERMS:\n- {躍進|やくしん} - rapid advance (opposite)\n- {発展|はってん} - development, progress\n- {成長|せいちょう} - growth\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {滞|とどこお}る - to stagnate (verb)\n- {行|い}き{詰|づ}まり - deadlock, impasse\n- {膠着|こうちゃく} - deadlock, stalemate\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral to formal. Common in news, economics, and weather reports.",
